2. Factory Pattern
          Purpose:    Hide object creation logic.
          
          Problem:
                    Payment payment = new CreditCardPayment();
          
                -Adding more types becomes messy.
          
          Solution:

          interface Payment {
              void pay();
          }
          class CreditCardPayment
                  implements Payment {
          }
          class UpiPayment
                  implements Payment {
          }
          
          Factory:
          
                    public class PaymentFactory {
                    
                        public static Payment getPayment(
                                String type) {
                    
                            if(type.equals("UPI"))
                                return new UpiPayment();
                    
                            return new CreditCardPayment();
                        }
                    }
          
          Usage:
                     Payment payment =  PaymentFactory.getPayment("UPI");

          Interview Question:   Why Factory?
          
          Answer:
                    Encapsulates creation logic
                    Reduces coupling
                    Supports OCP

